AnomalyBriefAggregates.description:
Exact server-computed evidence supplied to the LLM. Revenue responses
require revenue_scope and use its one selected currency throughout;
event-count responses omit revenue_scope.

CampaignAssuranceSourceClass.description:
`deterministic` is versioned rule-based analysis of exact frozen MIME;
`modeled` is a recorded prediction, not an inbox provider observation;
`controlled_observation` applies only to its named seed environment.

DataSufficiencyReport.description:
Tenant-wide rollup of which predictions are reliable per profile
bucket (SUB-129). Read from profile_prediction_sufficiency_rollup;
percentages are derived on read (count / total).

latestPolicy.description:
Newest in-window report's normalized `p=` observation for an
explicitly selected domain. Omitted for tenant-wide or empty scope;
not a live DNS record and not a replacement recommendation.

EmailHealthRecommendation.description:
Advisory action derived by `postwave-email-health-v1`. `blocked` is
authoritative when consent or an active suppression forbids sending;
no positive grade or activity evidence can override it.

FactContractRequiredFactV1.description:
Exactly one typed value member is required and must match `type`:
text/location/code use `text_value`; datetime uses `datetime_value`;
money uses `money_value`; percentage/quantity use `number_value`; URL
uses `url_value`. Percentage is bounded to 0–100 with unit `%`;
quantity is nonnegative and requires a unit.

MigrationSourcePlatform.description:
Source adapter accepted by migration route path parameters. The
subscriber-origin marker `mailchimp_api` is deliberately excluded;
Mailchimp migrations use `mailchimp` and OAuth.

post.description:
Replaces the token-bound subscriber's explicit choices for the supplied
unique topic UUIDs. Each topic must belong to the capability's tenant;
unknown or cross-tenant identifiers fail atomically.

