get.description:
Returns every conversion site key owned by the tenant, newest first,
including revoked keys. Plaintext is never returned by this read;
`prefix` is display-only and cannot be used for ingestion.

Returns cached anonymous platform-wide 30-day averages when available.
Otherwise it returns explicitly labelled illustrative 2024 averages;
the `note` field always identifies the provenance.

schema.example:
event: stats
data: {"range":"30d","subscribers_total":1200,...}

event: error
data: {"code":"analytics_stream_unavailable","message":"Live analytics could not be refreshed. Reconnect to retry."}

action_kind.description:
The granular kind for action nodes (add_tag, remove_tag, …);
every other node type reports its own type (wait, branch,
send_email, webhook).

